    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 7th Grade (CEFR: A2.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Importance of Water</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How We Use Water Everyday</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Concept: Guide peers through setting up a classroom activity. Concept: Assist in explaining the rules of a classroom game.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can guide peers through setting up a classroom activity about water conservation (e.g., "First, place the poster about saving water on the wall. Then, arrange the chairs for the group discussion.")
Can assist in explaining the rules of a classroom game focused on water usage (e.g., "In this game, you have to match pictures of water-saving actions with their descriptions. The team with the most matches wins.")
Can help classmates understand steps for a science experiment on water filtration (e.g., "First, pour the dirty water into the filter. Then, watch how the clean water comes out from the bottom.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing pictures of different ways people use water daily (e.g., drinking, washing, watering plants). Ask students: "How do we use water everyday? Why is saving water important?" Activate prior knowledge from previous lessons on water conservation using words like 'potable', 'resource', 'save', 'waste'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher explains the day's focus on guiding and explaining. "Today, we will learn how to clearly explain tasks and guide our friends. For example, 'First, open your books. Then, read the first paragraph.' Notice how I use 'first' and 'then' to make it clear." The teacher models pronunciation of stress patterns in compound words like "rainwater" and "water-saving" when giving instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of giving instructions.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do you read first or open your books first?" (Expected answer: "Open books first.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are the instructions clear or confusing?" (Expected answer: "Clear.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 7-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Importance of Water")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short, clear set of instructions for a "Water Conservation Poster" activity, using sequence words and relevant vocabulary. The instructions could be a simple flow chart or numbered steps on a slide. Example: "How to Design a Water Conservation Poster: 1. First, choose a water-saving action (e.g., turning off the tap). 2. Then, draw a picture showing this action. 3. Next, write a slogan using 'If...then...' (e.g., 'If you turn off the tap, you will save water.'). 4. Finally, explain why it's important (e.g., 'We save water because it is an essential resource for drinking.')."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Can understand and follow multi-step instructions related to a familiar topic (water conservation) and understand explanations about its importance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students match the instruction steps with corresponding images of a poster being created.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False questions about the instructions: "True or False: You write the slogan first." "True or False: We draw a picture of a polluted river for this poster."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice giving and interpreting instructions and explanations related to water conservation, focusing on sequence (first, then, next, finally), expressing purpose (for + verb + ing), cause-effect (because), and conditional statements (first conditional).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ol>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice: "Complete the Steps":</b> Teacher provides sentences with blanks for sequence words and key vocabulary. Students complete them. Example: "_____, turn off the (tap) when brushing your teeth. _____, collect (rainwater) for your plants. If we do this, we _____ (will save) a lot of water _____ (because) it is a limited resource." (Focus on 'forecast' and 'important' pronunciation when reviewing answers.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice: "Purpose and Reason Chains":</b> Students rephrase simple actions into explanations. Teacher gives an action, students add purpose or reason. Example: "We use a filter (for purifying water)." "We conserve water (because it is essential)." "We turn off the tap (for saving potable water)."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction: "Explain a Water-Saving Habit":</b> In pairs, students take turns explaining a specific water-saving habit (e.g., how to wash dishes efficiently, how to take a shorter shower). One student explains the steps and reasons, using sequence words, first conditional, and 'because'/'for + verb + ing'. The partner listens and asks clarifying questions, then confirms understanding. Example: "First, wet your hands. Then, turn off the tap for saving water. If you leave it on, you will waste a lot."</li>
                    </ol>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Importance of Water")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: "PSA Group Plan Explanation"</b> (Connecting to the 21st Century Skills Project: Water Conservation PSA). Students work in their established PSA groups. Each group needs to collaboratively explain their PSA plan. Students will take on mediation roles:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One student (or a pair) will <b>guide peers</b> through setting up a part of their PSA (e.g., "First, we will draw the initial scene for our PSA. Then, we will write the main message.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Another student will <b>assist in explaining the "rules"</b> or key messages of their PSA, especially how they will use the first conditional to show consequences. (e.g., "In our PSA, the main idea is to show that 'If we don't fix the leak, we will waste potable water.'"). They will also explain the purpose: "We are making this PSA for informing people about water shortages."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A third student helps clarify vocabulary or concepts to ensure all group members understand (e.g., "This means if there's a drought, water won't be available, so we must conserve it wisely."). They use "because" to explain why certain actions or messages are important.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in explaining, clarity in guiding, collaborative interaction, and systematic use of First Conditional, 'for + verb + ing', 'because', and target vocabulary (shortage, conserve, filter, limited resource, daily, carefully).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 12-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on clarity, coherence, and use of target linguistic features during group explanations and guidance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group briefly presents a 1-minute segment of their PSA plan, with specific students taking turns to (1) guide the class through one visual or setup element (e.g., "First, imagine this is our poster. Then, we will point to the text.") and (2) explain one core message or rule of their PSA clearly, using the first conditional, 'for + verb + ing', or 'because'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of explanations and guidance (Mediation skill).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate and intelligible pronunciation, especially for compound words (e.g., 'water-saving', 'forecast').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of the First Conditional to express cause-effect.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of 'for + verb + ing' to express purpose.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of 'because' to express cause.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of target vocabulary (water, resource, shortage, tap, conserve, available, purify, important).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Evidence of collaborative interaction and effective communication within the group.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I explain my part of the PSA plan clearly so my classmates could understand?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of explaining instructions or guiding others do I need to practice more?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 6-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did our group work together to explain our PSA, and how did we ensure everyone understood our message about water conservation?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new vocabulary or grammar structures did you find most useful for guiding and explaining today?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well during the mediation activities? Were students able to effectively guide their peers and explain complex ideas about the PSA project? What specific linguistic challenges arose (e.g., proper use of conditionals, sequencing adverbs)? What adjustments or additional scaffolds (e.g., sentence frames for explanations, visual cues for sequence) are needed for future mediation tasks with this group or similar topics?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the "How We Use Water Everyday" theme and the "Water Conservation Public Service Announcement" project. The skills developed in mediating and explaining will be valuable for future collaborative projects and presentations in subsequent units, where students will apply their 21st-century communication skills to new themes and scenarios.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>